(   [Problem Statement]: Detail array initialization techniques in ANSI C, contrasting full initialization, partial initialization, and C99 designated initializers.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Array Initialization Techniques in ANSI C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Full Static Initialization:) Tj
T*
(   - Elements are enclosed within curly braces separated by commas:) Tj
T*
(   int prime_factors[5] = {2, 3, 5, 7, 11};) Tj
T*
(   - Array Size Inference: If size dimension is omitted, compiler computes size from initializer) Tj
T*
(   count:) Tj
T*
(   int primes[] = {2, 3, 5, 7, 11}; /* Automatically sized to 5 elements */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Partial Initialization and Zero-Fill Guarantee:) Tj
T*
(   - If fewer initializers are supplied than the declared capacity:) Tj
T*
(   int buffer[10] = {1, 2, 3};) Tj
T*
(   - ISO C Guarantee: The remaining unspecified elements are AUTOMATICALLY INITIALIZED TO ZERO!) Tj
T*
(   - Idiomatic Zero-Clear:) Tj
T*
(   int zero_array[100] = {0}; /* Guaranteed all 100 elements are zeroed */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Uninitialized Automatic Arrays Trap:) Tj
T*
(   - Declaring int data[50]; inside a function without an initializer leaves memory uninitialized.) Tj
T*
(   - Reading data[i] retrieves indeterminate garbage bits leftover from previous stack frames,) Tj
T*
(   causing non-deterministic application bugs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. C99 Designated Initializers:) Tj
T*
(   - Allows explicit initialization of designated array indices in any arbitrary order:) Tj
T*
(   int lookup_table[10] = { [2] = 200, [7] = 700, [4] = 400 };) Tj
T*
(   - Any indices not explicitly designated are automatically zeroed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Demonstrative ANSI C Program:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   /* 1. Partial initialization with zero-fill */) Tj
T*
(   int partial_arr[6] = {10, 20};) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Partial array: "\);) Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 0; i < 6; i++\) printf\("%d ", partial_arr[i]\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("\\n"\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* 2. C99 Designated initializer */) Tj
T*
(   int codon_weights[8] = {[0] = 15, [4] = 95, [7] = 120};) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Designated array: "\);) Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 0; i < 8; i++\) printf\("[%d]:%d ", i, codon_weights[i]\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("\\n"\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return 0;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
