(   ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException.) Tj
T*
(   - In ANSI C, THERE IS ZERO RUNTIME ARRAY BOUNDS CHECKING!) Tj
T*
(   - Philosophy: C prioritizes maximum hardware execution velocity. Adding runtime boundary checks) Tj
T*
(   on every pointer arithmetic instruction incurs heavy CPU branch overhead.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Out-of-Bounds Memory Corruption:) Tj
T*
(   - When code accesses arr[15] on an array of size 10:) Tj
T*
(   Calculated address: Base + 15 * sizeof\(int\).) Tj
T*
(   The CPU reads or writes directly to whatever memory resides at that offset!) Tj
T*
(   - Stack Buffer Overflow: Overwriting stack memory corrupts adjacent local variables, stack) Tj
T*
(   canaries, saved frame pointers \(EBP/RBP\), and the function's Return Address.) Tj
T*
(   - Exploitation: Attackers supply oversized inputs that overwrite the return address with the) Tj
T*
(   address of malicious shellcode, hijacking control of the process.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complete Demonstration Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   void vulnerable_function\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   int target_variable = 0;) Tj
T*
(   int array_buffer[4] = {10, 20, 30, 40};) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   printf\("Target variable BEFORE overflow: %d\\n", target_variable\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Out-of-bounds write: Writing beyond index 3 */) Tj
T*
(   /* On typical stack layouts, index 4 or 5 aliases target_variable! */) Tj
T*
(   array_buffer[4] = 9999; /* UNDEFINED BEHAVIOR! */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   printf\("Target variable AFTER overflow: %d \(CORRUPTED!\)\\n", target_variable\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   vulnerable_function\(\);) Tj
T*
(   return 0;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Defensive Standards:) Tj
T*
(   - Always validate indices: if \(index >= 0 && index < ARRAY_SIZE\).) Tj
T*
(   - Use compile-time warnings: gcc -Wall -Wextra -Warray-bounds -fsanitize=address.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
