(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Multi-Dimensional Arrays in C, detailing 2D row-major layout, memory offset formulas, and matrix transformations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Multi-Dimensional Arrays and 2D Row-Major Layout:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition and Conceptualization:) Tj
T*
(   - A multi-dimensional array is an 'array of arrays'.) Tj
T*
(   - A 2D array int M[ROWS][COLS] represents ROWS individual 1D arrays, each containing COLS) Tj
T*
(   elements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Row-Major Ordering in Memory:) Tj
T*
(   - Physical computer RAM is strictly 1-dimensional \(linear address space\).) Tj
T*
(   - C lays out multidimensional arrays in Row-Major Order:) Tj
T*
(   All elements of Row 0 are stored contiguously, followed immediately by all elements of Row 1,) Tj
T*
ET

