BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to perform Matrix Multiplication C = A x B, explaining dimensional constraints and cache locality.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Matrix Multiplication Algorithm and Cache Optimization:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Constraints:) Tj
T*
(   - Matrix A has dimension \(M x K\); Matrix B has dimension \(K x N\).) Tj
T*
(   - Inner dimensions MUST match \(columns of A == rows of B == K\).) Tj
T*
(   - Result matrix C has dimension \(M x N\).) Tj
T*
(   - Dot Product Recurrence: C[i][j] = Sum_{k=0}^{K-1} \(A[i][k] * B[k][j]\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Computational Complexity:) Tj
T*
(   - Three nested loops: Outer loop i \(M iterations\), middle loop j \(N iterations\), inner loop k) Tj
T*
(   \(K iterations\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total operations: M * N * K multiplications and additions. For N x N square matrices: O\(N^3\)) Tj
T*
(   time complexity.) Tj
T*
ET

