(   In-Place Matrix Transposition:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Definition:) Tj
T*
(   The transpose of matrix A, denoted A^T, swaps rows and columns:) Tj
T*
(   A^T[i][j] = A[j][i].) Tj
T*
(   - Main diagonal elements \(where i == j\) remain completely unchanged.) Tj
T*
(   - Non-diagonal elements are symmetric reflections across the main diagonal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. In-Place Swapping Strategy:) Tj
T*
(   - For an N x N square matrix, swapping can be performed in-place using O\(1\) auxiliary space.) Tj
T*
(   - Traversal Boundary: Loop 'i' from 0 to N-1, and loop 'j' strictly from \(i + 1\) to N-1) Tj
T*
(   \(strictly upper triangle\).) Tj
T*
(   - Swap A[i][j] with A[j][i].) Tj
T*
(   - Caution: If 'j' loops from 0 to N-1, elements are swapped twice, returning the matrix to its) Tj
T*
(   original state!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   #define N 4) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
