(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to implement Linear Search and Binary Search on an array, analyzing comparative search benchmarks.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Linear Search vs Binary Search Implementation and Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Linear Search:) Tj
T*
(   - Iterates sequentially through each element from index 0 to N-1.) Tj
T*
(   - Works on both unsorted and sorted datasets.) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(1\) best case, O\(N\) average and worst case.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Binary Search:) Tj
T*
(   - Operates on pre-sorted arrays via divide-and-conquer.) Tj
T*
(   - Compares query target with midpoint element. Halves search space each iteration.) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(1\) best case, O\(log N\) worst case.) Tj
T*
(   - For N = 1,000,000 items: Linear search takes up to 1,000,000 comparisons; Binary search takes) Tj
T*
(   at most 20 comparisons!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int linear_search\(const int *arr, int size, int target, int *comparisons\) {) Tj
T*
(   *comparisons = 0;) Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 0; i < size; i++\) {) Tj
T*
(   \(*comparisons\)++;) Tj
T*
(   if \(arr[i] == target\) return i;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   return -1;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int binary_search\(const int *arr, int size, int target, int *comparisons\) {) Tj
T*
(   *comparisons = 0;) Tj
T*
(   int low = 0, high = size - 1;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   while \(low <= high\) {) Tj
T*
(   \(*comparisons\)++;) Tj
T*
(   int mid = low + \(high - low\) / 2;) Tj
T*
(   if \(arr[mid] == target\) {) Tj
T*
(   return mid;) Tj
T*
(   } else if \(target < arr[mid]\) {) Tj
T*
(   high = mid - 1;) Tj
T*
(   } else {) Tj
T*
(   low = mid + 1;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   return -1;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
