(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to implement Bubble Sort with an early-termination swap flag optimization, analyzing best and worst cases.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Bubble Sort with Early-Termination Flag Optimization:) Tj
T*
(   1. Algorithmic Principle:) Tj
T*
(   - Passes through the array repeatedly, comparing adjacent pairs \(arr[j], arr[j+1]\).) Tj
T*
(   - If arr[j] > arr[j+1], they are swapped.) Tj
T*
(   - After pass 'i', the largest remaining unsorted element 'bubbles up' to its correct position) Tj
T*
(   \(N - 1 - i\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Early Termination Flag Optimization:) Tj
T*
(   - Problem: Standard bubble sort continues executing all N*\(N-1\)/2 comparisons even if the array) Tj
T*
(   becomes fully sorted early!) Tj
T*
(   - Solution: Introduce a boolean flag 'swapped'. Set swapped = false before each pass.) Tj
T*
(   - If any swap occurs, set swapped = true.) Tj
T*
(   - If a complete pass finishes without a single swap, THE ARRAY IS PROVABLY SORTED! Break out of) Tj
T*
(   loop immediately!) Tj
T*
(   - Best-Case Time Complexity: Reduces from O\(N^2\) to O\(N\) linear time on already sorted data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdbool.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   void bubble_sort_optimized\(int *arr, int n, int *total_passes\) {) Tj
T*
(   *total_passes = 0;) Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++\) {) Tj
T*
(   bool swapped = false;) Tj
T*
(   \(*total_passes\)++;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   for \(int j = 0; j < n - 1 - i; j++\) {) Tj
T*
(   if \(arr[j] > arr[j + 1]\) {) Tj
T*
(   int temp = arr[j];) Tj
T*
(   arr[j] = arr[j + 1];) Tj
T*
(   arr[j + 1] = temp;) Tj
T*
(   swapped = true;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
ET

