(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Kadane's Algorithm for finding the maximum contiguous subarray sum in O\(N\) time with code and tracing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Kadane's Algorithm for Maximum Subarray Sum:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Statement:) Tj
T*
(   Given an array of integers containing positive and negative values, find the contiguous) Tj
T*
(   subarray having the maximum possible sum.) Tj
T*
(   Brute-force approach tests all O\(N^2\) subarrays.) Tj
T*
(   Kadane's algorithm solves it in a single pass: O\(N\) time and O\(1\) space!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Dynamic Programming Logic:) Tj
T*
(   At each index 'i', we decide whether to:) Tj
T*
(   a. Extend the existing contiguous subarray: max_ending_here + arr[i]) Tj
T*
(   b. Start a brand new subarray beginning at arr[i]: arr[i]) Tj
T*
(   Recurrence:) Tj
T*
(   max_ending_here = max\(arr[i], max_ending_here + arr[i]\)) Tj
T*
(   max_so_far = max\(max_so_far, max_ending_here\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int kadane_max_subarray\(const int *arr, int n, int *start_idx, int *end_idx\) {) Tj
T*
(   int max_so_far = arr[0];) Tj
T*
(   int max_ending_here = arr[0];) Tj
T*
(   int s = 0;) Tj
T*
(   *start_idx = 0;) Tj
T*
(   *end_idx = 0;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 1; i < n; i++\) {) Tj
T*
(   if \(arr[i] > max_ending_here + arr[i]\) {) Tj
T*
(   max_ending_here = arr[i];) Tj
T*
(   s = i; /* Reset start index */) Tj
T*
(   } else {) Tj
T*
(   max_ending_here += arr[i];) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   if \(max_ending_here > max_so_far\) {) Tj
T*
(   max_so_far = max_ending_here;) Tj
T*
(   *start_idx = s;) Tj
T*
(   *end_idx = i;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   return max_so_far;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   int hydro_scores[] = {-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4};) Tj
T*
(   int n = sizeof\(hydro_scores\) / sizeof\(hydro_scores[0]\);) Tj
T*
(   int start = 0, end = 0;) Tj
T*
