T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Array Rotation via the Triple Reverse Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem:) Tj
T*
(   Rotate an array of N elements to the right by K positions.) Tj
T*
(   Example: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] rotated right by K=3 becomes [5, 6, 7, 1, 2, 3, 4].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Triple Reverse Invariant:) Tj
T*
(   First normalize K: K = K % N.) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Reverse the entire array [0...N-1].) Tj
T*
(   [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] -> [7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1]) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Reverse the first K elements [0...K-1].) Tj
T*
(   [7, 6, 5] -> [5, 6, 7]) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Reverse the remaining \(N - K\) elements [K...N-1].) Tj
T*
(   [4, 3, 2, 1] -> [1, 2, 3, 4]) Tj
T*
(   Result: [5, 6, 7, 1, 2, 3, 4]!) Tj
T*
(   Time Complexity: Exactly O\(N\) comparisons and swaps. Auxiliary Space: O\(1\) constant.) Tj
