(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Needleman-Wunsch algorithm for global DNA sequence alignment using a 2D dynamic programming array.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Needleman-Wunsch Global Alignment Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   1. Bioinformatics Background:) Tj
T*
(   Published in 1970 by Saul Needleman and Christian Wunsch.) Tj
T*
(   Computes the optimal global alignment between two biological sequences across their entire) Tj
T*
(   lengths using Dynamic Programming.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Matrix Initialization and Recurrence:) Tj
T*
(   Given sequence A of length M, sequence B of length N:) Tj
T*
(   Allocate 2D DP matrix F of dimension \(M + 1\) x \(N + 1\):) Tj
T*
(   - F[0][0] = 0) Tj
T*
(   - F[i][0] = i * GapPenalty \(gap along sequence B\)) Tj
T*
(   - F[0][j] = j * GapPenalty \(gap along sequence A\)) Tj
T*
(   Recurrence Relation for cell F[i][j]:) Tj
T*
(   F[i][j] = MAX\() Tj
T*
(   F[i - 1][j - 1] + S\(A[i-1], B[j-1]\), /* Diagonal: Match or Mismatch */) Tj
T*
(   F[i - 1][j] + GapPenalty, /* Up: Deletion in B \(Gap in B\) */) Tj
T*
