(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the two-pointer approach for finding a pair of elements in a sorted array that sum to a target value S.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Two-Pointer Sum Search in Sorted Arrays:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem:) Tj
T*
(   Given sorted array arr[0...N-1] and target sum S, find if two elements satisfy arr[i] + arr[j]) Tj
T*
(   == S.) Tj
T*
(   Brute-force testing all pairs takes O\(N^2\) time.) Tj
T*
(   The Two-Pointer approach solves it in O\(N\) linear time and O\(1\) space!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Operational Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   Initialize two pointers: left = 0 \(smallest\), right = N - 1 \(largest\).) Tj
T*
(   Loop while \(left < right\):) Tj
T*
(   - Current sum = arr[left] + arr[right].) Tj
T*
(   - If current sum == S: Pair found!) Tj
T*
(   - If current sum < S: We need a larger sum, so increment left \(left++\).) Tj
T*
(   - If current sum > S: We need a smaller sum, so decrement right \(right--\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdbool.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   bool find_pair_sum\(const int *arr, int n, int target, int *val1, int *val2\) {) Tj
T*
(   int left = 0, right = n - 1;) Tj
T*
(   while \(left < right\) {) Tj
T*
(   int sum = arr[left] + arr[right];) Tj
T*
(   if \(sum == target\) {) Tj
T*
(   *val1 = arr[left];) Tj
T*
(   *val2 = arr[right];) Tj
T*
(   return true;) Tj
T*
(   } else if \(sum < target\) {) Tj
T*
(   left++;) Tj
T*
(   } else {) Tj
T*
(   right--;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   return false;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   int sorted_mw[] = {120, 180, 240, 310, 450, 520, 680};) Tj
T*
(   int n = sizeof\(sorted_mw\) / sizeof\(sorted_mw[0]\);) Tj
T*
(   int target_mw = 690;) Tj
T*
(   int v1 = 0, v2 = 0;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
