(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to compute the trace \(sum of main diagonal elements\) of a square matrix.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Trace of a Square Matrix in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Definition:) Tj
T*
(   The trace of an N x N square matrix A, denoted tr\(A\), is the sum of the elements along its main) Tj
T*
(   diagonal:) Tj
T*
(   tr\(A\) = Sum_{i=0}^{N-1} A[i][i] = A[0][0] + A[1][1] + ... + A[N-1][N-1].) Tj
T*
(   Properties: tr\(A + B\) = tr\(A\) + tr\(B\); tr\(c * A\) = c * tr\(A\); tr\(A * B\) = tr\(B * A\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   #define N 4) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   long long compute_matrix_trace\(const int matrix[N][N]\) {) Tj
T*
(   long long trace_sum = 0;) Tj
T*
(   /* Single loop iterating along main diagonal \(O\(N\) time\) */) Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 0; i < N; i++\) {) Tj
T*
