(   - Modern CPUs load memory from RAM into L1/L2/L3 caches in discrete 64-byte blocks called Cache) Tj
T*
(   Lines.) Tj
T*
(   - Spatial Locality: Accessing address X automatically loads X+1, X+2, ..., X+15 into high-speed) Tj
T*
(   cache.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Row-Major Traversal \(Stride-1, High Spatial Locality\):) Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 0; i < ROWS; i++\)) Tj
T*
(   for \(int j = 0; j < COLS; j++\)) Tj
T*
(   sum += M[i][j];) Tj
T*
(   - Successive memory accesses are adjacent in RAM.) Tj
T*
(   - Accessing M[i][0] fetches M[i][0] through M[i][15] into L1 cache. The next 15 loop iterations) Tj
T*
(   hit the L1 cache in ~1 nanosecond!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Column-Major Traversal \(Strided, Cache Trashing\):) Tj
T*
(   for \(int j = 0; j < COLS; j++\)) Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 0; i < ROWS; i++\)) Tj
T*
(   sum += M[i][j];) Tj
T*
(   - Successive accesses jump across entire rows \(offset of COLS * 4 bytes\).) Tj
T*
(   - If COLS is large \(e.g. 4096 ints = 16 KB\), every single access hits a different cache line,) Tj
T*
(   incurring an L3 cache miss or RAM access penalty \(~50-100 nanoseconds\)!) Tj
T*
(   - Row-major traversal is often 10x to 20x faster than column-major traversal in C!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
